node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
# The web client's own tree and build output. The two lines above already match
# at any depth, so these are redundant to git and deliberate to a reader: this
# repository holds TWO dependency trees, and the second one is not an accident
# somebody should be tempted to commit.
apps/web/node_modules/
apps/web/dist/
.env
# The droplet's environment file, which holds the Anthropic key, the Telegram
# token and the Firebase pair. `docker-compose.deploy.yml` reads it; its layout
# is in docs/deploy-digitalocean.md and only the layout belongs in git.
.env.deploy
*.log
# Corpus dumps are local measurement scratch — the full 32-day pull is 9.8 MB
# across eleven fields and the ambiguity-scope cache beside it is 1,259 files.
# ONE exception is tracked, and it has to be: `filing-outcome.spec.ts` and
# `category-group.spec.ts` assert against all 17,442 rows, so with the corpus
# ignored those eleven tests could only ever pass on the machine holding the
# dump — they failed in CI from the day CI existed. The tracked slice carries
# the three fields those specs read and nothing else: 3.6 MB, ~600 KB packed.
# Ignore the CONTENTS rather than the directory; git does not descend into an
# ignored directory, so `!data/corpus/x` under `data/corpus/` would not work.
data/corpus/*
!data/corpus/05-07-2026_05-08-2026.summaries.jsonl
.superpowers/
.idea/
.vscode/
test-results/
playwright-report/
